{"packet_id":"D005-01","doc_id":"D005","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California tenant screening fee cap and refund rules","requirement":"A landlord's screening fee may not exceed the annual cap; the landlord must give a receipt, itemized costs and any unused-portion refund, use a reusable report if provided, and refund unselected applicants or charge none.","key_value":"$68.96 (2026)","coverage_conditions":"All residential rental applicants in California; applies whenever a landlord charges a screening fee.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"The maximum tenant screening fee for 2026 is $68.96","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D005-01","doc_id":"D005","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley tenant screening fee rights disclosure (BMC 13.78.010)","requirement":"A Berkeley owner or agent who charges a screening fee must give the applicant, in the application or a separate pre-fee disclosure, a clear tenant screening fee rights statement and the maximum fee cap under California Civil Code 1950.6(b).","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property in Berkeley where the owner charges a fee to purchase a credit report or process an application.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code § 13.78.010","quoted_span":"the owner must provide, either in the rental application or in a separate disclosure before receiving the fee, a clear and conspicuous tenant screening fee rights statement and a statement of the maximum fee cap permitted under California Civil Code Section 1950.6(b)","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D005-01","doc_id":"D005","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley ban on non-refundable application fees for existing tenancies (BMC 13.78.016)","requirement":"A Berkeley owner or agent may not charge an existing tenant any non-refundable fee to renew a tenancy, including fees to remove a departing roommate or to add or replace a roommate in the household.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Existing tenants of residential rental property in Berkeley, including roommate additions, replacements or departures.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code § 13.78.016","quoted_span":"An owner of residential rental property (or the owner’s agent) cannot charge a non-refundable fee to any existing tenant for the purpose of renewing a tenancy, in whole or in part, including any fee associated with the departure of a roommate or to request to add or replace a roommate in a pre-existing household.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D005-01","doc_id":"D005","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Chapter 13.78 applies despite contrary lease terms (BMC 13.78.018)","requirement":"Chapter 13.78 applies to all Berkeley residential rental agreements regardless of contrary lease language, and any lease provision that violates the chapter is unenforceable.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All residential rental agreements in Berkeley.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code § 13.78.018","quoted_span":"Chapter 13.78 applies to all residential rental agreements regardless of any contractual language in any rental agreement or lease to the contrary. Any provision of an existing rental agreement or lease that violates the provisions of this chapter are unenforceable.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
